{"name":"Cultured Pearl","hex":"#e5dcd6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cultured","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Learned in the ways of civilized society; civilized; refined.","Artificially developed."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of culture"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cultured"},{"term":"pearl","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shelly concretion, usually rounded, and having a brilliant luster, with varying tints, found in the mantle, or between the mantle and shell, of certain bivalve mollusks, especially in the pearl oysters and river mussels, and sometimes in certain univalves. It is usually due to a secretion of shelly substance around some irritating foreign particle. Its substance is the same as nacre, or mother-of-pearl. Round lustrous pearls are used in jewellery.\nNacre; mother-of-pearl.\n A white color inspired by the shade of pearls.","Nacre; mother-of-pearl."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To set or adorn with pearls, or with mother-of-pearl.","To cause to resemble pearls in shape; to make into small round grains."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pearl"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cultured pearl","blocks":[{"text":"Cultured pearls are pearls which are formed within a cultured pearl sac with human intervention in the interior of productive living molluscs in a variety of conditions depending upon the mollusc and the goals. Having the same material as natural pearls, cultured pearls can be cultivated in seawater or freshwater bodies. Over 95% of the pearls available on the market are cultured pearls."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Akoya_pearl.jpg/330px-Akoya_pearl.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cultured_pearl"},{"title":"Culture","blocks":[{"text":"Culture is a concept that encompasses the social behavior, institutions, and norms found in human societies, as well as the knowledge, beliefs, arts, laws, customs, capabilities, attitudes, and habits of the individuals in these groups. Culture often originates from or is attributed to a specific region or location."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/9_Bisonte_Magdaleniense_pol%C3%ADcromo.jpg/330px-9_Bisonte_Magdaleniense_pol%C3%ADcromo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Culture"},{"title":"Pearl","blocks":[{"text":"A pearl is a hard, shiny object produced within the soft tissue of a living shelled mollusk. Like the shell of a mollusk, a pearl is composed of calcium carbonate in a crystalline form, which is deposited in concentric layers. More commercially valuable pearls are perfectly round and smooth, but many other shapes, known as baroque pearls, can occur. The highest quality of natural pearls have been highly valued as gemstones and objects of beauty for many centuries. In literature, pearls have become a metaphor for something rare, fine, admirable, and valuable."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Various_pearls.jpg/330px-Various_pearls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pearl"},{"title":"Pearl (color)","blocks":[{"text":"The color pearl is a pale tint of off-white. It is a representation of the average color of a pearl."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c3/PerlmuttAusst.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pearl_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/White_pearl_necklace.jpg/500px-White_pearl_necklace.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/White_pearl_necklace.jpg/500px-White_pearl_necklace.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"White pearl necklace","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWhite_pearl_necklace.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Perles_de_Tahiti_%281%29.JPG/500px-Perles_de_Tahiti_%281%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Perles_de_Tahiti_%281%29.JPG/500px-Perles_de_Tahiti_%281%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cultured dark Tahiti pearls — one of the pearls is cut to expose the manmade nucleus bead","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APerles_de_Tahiti_(1).JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Cultured_Mabe_pearl_in_shape_of_Buddha.jpg/500px-Cultured_Mabe_pearl_in_shape_of_Buddha.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Cultured_Mabe_pearl_in_shape_of_Buddha.jpg/1280px-Cultured_Mabe_pearl_in_shape_of_Buddha.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Cultured_Mabe_pearl_in_shape_of_Buddha.jpg/500px-Cultured_Mabe_pearl_in_shape_of_Buddha.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cultured Mabe pearl in the shape of a Buddha","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACultured_Mabe_pearl_in_shape_of_Buddha.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Bi_quyet_phan_biet_ngoc_trai_tu_nhien_va_nuoi_cay_1.png/250px-Bi_quyet_phan_biet_ngoc_trai_tu_nhien_va_nuoi_cay_1.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/84/Bi_quyet_phan_biet_ngoc_trai_tu_nhien_va_nuoi_cay_1.png?utm_sourc